Feature: Category Management
  As a user
  I want to create a category
  So that I can classify my tasks

  Background:
    Given the Todo Manager API is running
    And I have recorded the current category collection

  # Normal flow
  Scenario Outline: Create a category with a title and description
    When I create a category with title "<title>" and description "<description>"
    Then the response status should be 201
    And the saved category should have title "<title>" and description "<description>"

    Examples:
      | title      | description          |
      | Coursework | Tasks for my courses |

  # Alternate flow
  Scenario Outline: Create a category with only a title
    When I create a category with only the title "<title>"
    Then the response status should be 201
    And the saved category should have title "<title>" and an empty description

    Examples:
      | title    |
      | Personal |

  # Error flow
  Scenario Outline: Reject a category with an empty title
    When I try to create a category with an empty title and description "<description>"
    Then the response status should be 400
    And the category collection should be unchanged

    Examples:
      | description         |
      | Tasks for this week |



  # C02 — View categories

  # Normal flow
  Scenario Outline: C02 View the category list
    Given I have created a category named "<title>"
    When I request the category list
    Then the response status should be 200
    And the category list should include the category I last created

    Examples:
      | title     |
      | Groceries |

  # Alternate flow
  Scenario Outline: C02 Filter categories by title
    Given I have created a category named "<other_title>"
    And I have created a category named "<title>"
    When I request categories with title "<title>"
    Then the response status should be 200
    And the category list should include the category I last created
    And every returned category should have title "<title>"

    Examples:
      | title   | other_title |
      | Reading | Errands     |

  # Error flow
  Scenario Outline: C02 Reject an unsupported response format
    When I request the category list with Accept "<media_type>"
    Then the response status should be 406
    And the category collection should be unchanged

    Examples:
      | media_type       |
      | application/yaml |



        # C03 — Update a category

  # Normal flow
  Scenario Outline: C03 Rename an existing category
    Given I have created a category with title "<old_title>" and description "<description>"
    When I rename the saved category to "<new_title>"
    Then the response status should be 200
    And the saved category should have title "<new_title>" and description "<description>"

    Examples:
      | old_title | new_title     | description  |
      | Shopping  | Shopping List | Items to buy |

  # Alternate flow
  Scenario Outline: C03 Update only the category description
    Given I have created a category with title "<title>" and description "<old_description>"
    When I change the saved category description to "<new_description>"
    Then the response status should be 200
    And the saved category should have title "<title>" and description "<new_description>"

    Examples:
      | title   | old_description | new_description       |
      | Reading | Books to read   | Books to read in 2026 |

  # Error flow
  Scenario Outline: C03 Reject an empty category title during update
    Given I have created a category with title "<title>" and description "<description>"
    When I try to rename the saved category to an empty title
    Then the response status should be 400
    And the saved category should have title "<title>" and description "<description>"

    Examples:
      | title   | description       |
      | Errands | Tasks around town |


        # C04 — Retrieve a category by ID

  # Normal flow
  Scenario Outline: C04 Retrieve a category with a title and description
    Given I have created a category with title "<title>" and description "<description>"
    When I request the category I last created by ID
    Then the response status should be 200
    And the response should contain the requested category with title "<title>" and description "<description>"

    Examples:
      | title   | description      |
      | Fitness | Weekly workouts  |

  # Alternate flow
  Scenario Outline: C04 Retrieve a category created without a description
    Given I have created a category named "<title>"
    When I request the category I last created by ID
    Then the response status should be 200
    And the response should contain the requested category with title "<title>" and an empty description

    Examples:
      | title  |
      | Travel |

  # Error flow
  Scenario Outline: C04 Retrieve a category that no longer exists
    Given I have created a category named "<title>"
    And the category I last created has been deleted
    When I request the category I last created by ID
    Then the response status should be 404

    Examples:
      | title             |
      | Temporary Archive |


        # C05 — Delete a category

  # Normal flow
  Scenario Outline: C05 Delete an existing category
    Given I have created a category named "<title>"
    When I delete the category I last created
    Then the response status should be 200
    And the deleted category should no longer be retrievable

    Examples:
      | title       |
      | Old errands |

  # Alternate flow
  Scenario Outline: C05 Delete one category and keep another
    Given I have created a category named "<kept_title>"
    And I have created a category named "<deleted_title>"
    When I delete the category I last created
    Then the response status should be 200
    And the deleted category should no longer be retrievable
    And the first category I created should still have title "<kept_title>"

    Examples:
      | kept_title | deleted_title |
      | Keep notes | Old notes     |

  # Error flow
  Scenario Outline: C05 Reject deleting the same category twice
    Given I have created a category named "<title>"
    And the category I last created has been deleted
    When I delete the category I last created
    Then the response status should be 404
    And the category collection should be unchanged

    Examples:
      | title        |
      | Expired list |